  "summary": "After the Siloam Springs Board of Directors voted 6-1 to turn off the city's six Flock Safety license plate readers, police began disabling the cameras and covered them with black bags as a preemptive measure. Interim Chief Chase Fine said the department will continue investigations using other tools while a final decision on the Flock contract is pending.",
